# rockable.lang -- syntax highlighting, inline documentation and snippets
# for the Rockable input files (conf, shapes, drivingSystem, postpro).
#
# Read at start-up by the editors in prepro/; edit it to document a new
# keyword, no recompilation needed.
#
# Format
#   [keyword] name    a command word, highlighted as a keyword
#   [type] name       an enumerated value, highlighted as a type
#   [snippet] Title   a template; its body is every line up to the next [ ]
#   doc: first line   documentation of the entry just above; continuation
#     lines are indented by two spaces, blank lines are kept
#
# Outside of a doc or a snippet body, a line starting with '#' is a comment
# and blank lines are ignored.


# ===========================================================================
# Keywords
# ===========================================================================

[keyword] Rockable
doc: A conf-file always starts with the header: Rockable dd-mm-yyyy (e.g., Rockable 20-02-2017).
  Each time a noticeable change is made in the format, the date of this change is also changed
  in the header of the file. It has to be understood as the version of the format.

[keyword] t
doc: t [(double) value]

  Current time

[keyword] tmax
doc: tmax [(double) value]

  Maximum time (at the end of a simulation)

[keyword] dt
doc: dt [(double) value]

  Time step increment

[keyword] interVerlet
doc: interVerlet [(double) duration]

  Elapsed time between each update of the neighbor list (NL)

[keyword] interConf
doc: interConf [(double) duration]

  Elapsed time between each backup of the configuration

[keyword] DVerlet
doc: DVerlet [(double) distance]

  Increment size of the OBBs surrounding the rigid bodies

[keyword] dVerlet
doc: dVerlet [(double) distance]

  Increment size of the OBBs surrounding the sub-elements of the rigid bodies

[keyword] density
doc: density [(int)groupNumber] [(double) density]

  Set the density of all particles belonging to the group groupNumber

[keyword] gravity
doc: gravity [(vec3r) value]

   value = components of the gravity

[keyword] ParamsInInterfaces
doc: ParamsInInterfaces [0/1]

  States wether the parameters are embedded in the glued interfaces

[keyword] dynamicUpdateNL
doc: dynamicUpdateNL [0/1]

  If the dynamic update of the neighbor list is activated (set to 1), then an update will be made
  if the maximum distance of a body, since the last update, becomes larger than 'dispUpdateNL'.
  An update will also be made when the maximum rotation becomes larger than 'angleUpdateNL'

[keyword] dispUpdateNL
doc: dispUpdateNL [(double) distance]

  The maximum distance that any body is allowed to move without updating the NL

[keyword] angleUpdateNL
doc: angleUpdateNL [(double) angleDegree]

  The maximum angle that any body is allowed to rotate without updating the NL

[keyword] numericalDampingCoeff
doc: numericalDampingCoeff [(double) value]

  Cundall non-viscous numerical damping coefficient (typically between 0 and 1).
  At each step the accelerations are scaled by (1 - value) or (1 + value) depending
  on whether they oppose or follow the velocity, which damps the motion.
  Set to 0 to disable.

[keyword] VelocityBarrier
doc: VelocityBarrier [(double) value]

  Reference translational velocity above which a barrier force progressively slows
  the bodies down. The opposing force grows like (|v|/VelocityBarrier)^VelocityBarrierExponent.
  Set to 0 (default) to disable.

[keyword] AngularVelocityBarrier
doc: AngularVelocityBarrier [(double) value]

  Same as VelocityBarrier but applied to the angular velocity of the bodies.
  Set to 0 (default) to disable.

[keyword] VelocityBarrierExponent
doc: VelocityBarrierExponent [(double) value]

  Exponent used by the translational velocity barrier (see VelocityBarrier).
  The larger the exponent, the sharper the barrier.

[keyword] AngularVelocityBarrierExponent
doc: AngularVelocityBarrierExponent [(double) value]

  Exponent used by the angular velocity barrier (see AngularVelocityBarrier).

[keyword] Tempo
doc: Tempo [(string) target] ...

  Defines a time-evolving ('tempo') parameter interpolated between two times.
  Three forms are available:

    Tempo NDCoeff [command] [t1] [t2] [val1] [val2]
        drives the numericalDampingCoeff
    Tempo Inter [paramName] [group1] [group2] [command] [t1] [t2] [val1] [val2]
        drives an interaction parameter (e.g. knContact) between two groups
    Tempo Body [paramName] [group] [command] [t1] [t2] [val1] [val2]
        drives a body property (e.g. density) of a group

  'command' selects the interpolation profile between (t1,val1) and (t2,val2).

[keyword] forceLaw
doc: forceLaw [(string)Name]

  Select a model for the computation of forces.
  Possible Names are: 'Default', 'Avalanche', 'StickedLinks', 'GeoVisc' or 'BCM'.

[keyword] AddOrRemoveInteractions
doc: AddOrRemoveInteractions [(string) Name]

  Strategy used to detect which interactions must be created or deleted.
  Possible Names are: 'bruteForce' (default) or 'OBBtree'.

[keyword] UpdateNL
doc: UpdateNL [(string) Name]

  Strategy used to rebuild the neighbor list (NL).
  Possible Names are: 'bruteForce' (default) or 'linkCells'.

[keyword] Integrator
doc: Integrator [(string) Name]

  Time-integration scheme.
  Possible Names are: 'velocityVerlet' (default), 'Euler', 'Beeman' or 'RungeKutta4'.

[keyword] cellMinSizes
doc: cellMinSizes [(double) value]

  Minimum size of the cells used by the 'linkCells' neighbor-list strategy.

[keyword] boxForLinkCellsOpt
doc: boxForLinkCellsOpt [(int) 0/1]

  Selects the bounding box used to build the link-cells grid.
  0 (default): box surrounding all particles;
  1: box surrounding only the free (non-driven) bodies.

[keyword] ContactPartnership
doc: ContactPartnership [(string) Name]

  Model used to weight the contact stiffnesses when several sub-elements of two
  bodies interact at once (used by some force laws).
  Possible Names are: 'None' (default), 'NumberWeight', 'OverlapWeight' or 'SurfaceWeight'.

[keyword] preventCrossingLength
doc: preventCrossingLength [(double) value]

  If positive, enables a safeguard that prevents bodies from crossing/tunneling
  through each other when the overlap would exceed this characteristic length.

[keyword] initSpringJoint
doc: initSpringJoint [(int) ibody] [(vec3r) ipos0] [(int) jbody] [(vec3r) jpos0] [(double) stiffness]

  Create a linear spring joint between bodies ibody and jbody, anchored at the
  local positions ipos0 and jpos0, with the given stiffness.

# --- periodic cell (requires Rockable compiled with ROCKABLE_ENABLE_PERIODIC)

[keyword] usePeriodicCell
doc: usePeriodicCell [0/1]

  Enable (1) or disable (0) the periodic boundary cell.
  Requires Rockable compiled with ROCKABLE_ENABLE_PERIODIC.

[keyword] h
doc: h [(mat9r) matrix]

  The 3x3 matrix (9 components) defining the periodic cell (column vectors are the
  periodicity vectors).

[keyword] vh
doc: vh [(mat9r) matrix]

  Time derivative (velocity) of the periodic cell matrix 'h'.

[keyword] ah
doc: ah [(mat9r) matrix]

  Second time derivative (acceleration) of the periodic cell matrix 'h'.

[keyword] mh
doc: mh [(double) value]

  Mass ratio assigned to the periodic cell degrees of freedom.

[keyword] dh
doc: dh [(double) value]

  Numerical damping applied to the periodic cell.

[keyword] cellMomentumCorrection
doc: cellMomentumCorrection [0/1]

  Enable correction of the total momentum within the periodic cell.

[keyword] cellVelocityCorrection
doc: cellVelocityCorrection [0/1]

  Enable correction of the velocities within the periodic cell.

[keyword] useKineticStress
doc: useKineticStress [0/1]

  Include the kinetic (velocity fluctuation) contribution in the stress of the periodic cell.

# --- soft particles (requires Rockable compiled with ROCKABLE_ENABLE_SOFT_PARTICLES)

[keyword] useSoftParticles
doc: useSoftParticles [(double) Young] [(double) Poisson]

  Enable deformable (soft) particles with the given Young modulus and Poisson ratio.
  Requires Rockable compiled with ROCKABLE_ENABLE_SOFT_PARTICLES.

