  used by the BCM (Bonded Cell Model) force law.

[keyword] iconf
doc: iconf [(int) value]Number of the current configuration

[keyword] nDriven
doc: nDriven [(int) value]

  The value is the number of bodies, at the beginning of the list, that nDriven first bodies
  are fixed (all velocities imposed to zero), but if we want to set a velocity or a force/moment,
  some commands have to be added in a file named drivingSystem.txt

[keyword] shapeFile
doc: shapeFile [(string) path]

  Paths of the file that defines the shapes used.

[keyword] separator
doc: By default, the separator character in a conf-file is the 'space'
  but it can be changed to 'tab' or 'semicolon'

[keyword] glue_with_walls
doc: glue_with_walls [0/1]

  State wether the glue will be activated between driven and not-driven bodies
  when the command 'stickClusters' will be invoked

[keyword] precision
doc: precision [(int) value]

  Set the number of digits to be used in the conf-files

[keyword] Particles
doc: Particles [(int) numberOfParticles]

  REPEAT FOR EACH PARTICLE {
     [(string) shapeName] [(int) group] [(int) cluster] [(double) homothety]
     [(vec3r) position] [(vec3r) velocity] [(vec3r) acceleration]
     [(quat) angularPosition] [(vec3r) angularVelocity] [(vec3r) angularAcceleration]
  }

[keyword] Interactions
doc: Interactions [(int) numberOfInteractions]

  REPEAT FOR EACH INTERACTION {
     [(int) i] [(int) j] [(int) type] [(int) isub] [(int) jsub] [(vec3r) n] [(double) dn] [(vec3r) position]
     [(vec3r) relativeVelocity] [(double) fn] [(vec3r) ft] [(vec3r) mom] [(double) viscousDampingValue]
  }

[keyword] Interfaces
doc: Interfaces [(int)numberOfInterfaces]

  REPEAT FOR EACH INTERFACE {
     [(int) i] [(int) j] [(int) nbBonds]
     IF (ParamsInInterfaces is not 0) {
        [(double) kn] [(double) kt] [(double) kr] [(double) fn0] [(double) ft0] [(double) mom0] [(double) power]
     }
     REPEAT FOR EACH BOND { [(int) type] [(int) isub] [(int) jsub] }
  }

[keyword] DataExtractor
doc: DataExtractor [(string) Name] ...

  Adds a data extractor that records quantities during the simulation.
  Possible Names are: 'ClusterAABB', 'dnStat', 'DuoBalance', 'MeanVelocity' or 'TrackBody'.
  The remaining parameters depend on the chosen extractor.
  Kept for compatibility: prefer defining them in a file named 'dataExtractors.txt'.

[keyword] BodyForce
doc: BodyForce [(string) Name] ...

  Activates a body force applied to the particles.
  Possible Names are: 'AttractingPoint', 'PreferredDirection' or 'ViscousFluid'.
  The remaining parameters depend on the chosen body force.

# --- processing

[keyword] stickVerticesInClusters
doc: stickVerticesInClusters [(double) Epsilon]

  This command will add glued interfaces between bodies having
  the same cluster identifier. Only bonds between vertices (spheres)
  are added when the distance is less than Epsilon.

[keyword] stickVerticesInClustersMoments
doc: stickVerticesInClustersMoments [(double) Epsilon]

  Like stickVerticesInClusters, but the created bonds also transmit moments.
  Bonds between vertices (spheres) of a same cluster are added when the distance
  is less than Epsilon.

[keyword] stickClusters
doc: stickClusters [(double) Epsilon]

  This command will add glued interfaces between bodies having different cluster identifiers.
  Bonds are added when the distance is less than Epsilon.

[keyword] stickBCM
doc: stickBCM [(double) Epsilon]

  Create the bonded interfaces required by the BCM (Bonded Cell Model) force law
  between neighboring sub-elements closer than Epsilon.

[keyword] copyParamsToInterfaces
doc: copyParamsToInterfaces [(string) isInnerStr]

[keyword] setStiffnessRatioInterfaces
doc: setStiffnessRatioInterfaces [(double) ratio]

  Set the tangential-to-normal stiffness ratio kt/kn for every bond stored in the
  glued interfaces (only for parameters that are embedded in the Interfaces).

[keyword] setVariableStickParams
doc: setVariableStickParams [(string) paramName] [(string) isInnerStr] [(double) lambda] [(double) m] [(int) timeSeeded]

[keyword] randomlyOrientedVelocities
doc: randomlyOrientedVelocities [(double) velocity]

[keyword] randomlyOrientedVelocitiesClusters
doc: randomlyOrientedVelocitiesClusters [(double) velocity] [(int) option]

[keyword] setAllVelocities
doc: setAllVelocities [(vec3r) velocity]

  Set the same velocity vector to ALL free (non-driven) bodies.

[keyword] homothetyRange
doc: homothetyRange [(int) idFirst] [(int) idLast] [(double) hmin] [(double) hmax] [(int) timeSeeded]

  Assign to the bodies idFirst..idLast a homothety drawn from a uniform distribution
  in [hmin, hmax]. If timeSeeded is 1, the random generator is seeded with the current time.

[keyword] particlesClonage
doc: particlesClonage [(int) idFirst] [(int) idLast] [(vec3r) translation]

  Duplicate the bodies idFirst..idLast, shifting the clones by the translation vector.
  The clones receive new cluster identifiers.

# --- driving system

[keyword] Control
doc: Control [(string) mode] [(int) bodyNumber] [(double) value]

  where mode is either:
                       _x_Vel_, _y_Vel_, _z_Vel_,
                       _xrot_Vel_, _yrot_Vel_, _zrot_Vel_,
                       _x_For_, _y_For_, _z_For_,
                       _xrot_Mom_, _yrot_Mom_, _zrot_Mom_,
                       _xyzrot_Vel_, or _xyzrot_Mom_

  This is a simple solution to impose a constant velocity or force/moment to a body.
  Notice that bodyNumber needs to be lower than 'nDriven'

[keyword] Servo
doc: Servo [(string) Name] ...

  Activates a predefined servo-controller that drives a set of walls/bodies.
  The 'tritri*' servos (e.g. tritriIsostaticCompression, tritriBiaxialCompression,
  tritriCustom, tritriLodeAngle) expect the 6 wall body numbers
  (idXmin idXmax idYmin idYmax idZmin idZmax) followed by servo-specific parameters.
  Other servos: shaker, triangle_shaker, sawtooth_shaker, ramp.
  Servo commands are defined in the file 'drivingSystem.txt'.

[keyword] PeriodicLoading
doc: PeriodicLoading [(string) Name] ...

  Drive the periodic cell with a predefined loading.
  Example: 'PeriodicLoading IsotropicCompression [(double) pressure]'.
  Defined in the file 'drivingSystem.txt'.

# --- post-processing (postpro tool input files)

[keyword] PostProcessor
doc: PostProcessor [(string) Name] ...

  Adds a post-processor (used by the 'postpro' tool).
  Possible Names are: 'ClusterGranulo' or 'ParticleStress'.

[keyword] firstConf
doc: firstConf [(int) value]

  Number of the first conf-file to post-process.

[keyword] lastConf
doc: lastConf [(int) value]

  Number of the last conf-file to post-process.

[keyword] stepConf
doc: stepConf [(int) value]

  Step between two processed conf-files.

[keyword] ConfVolumes
doc: ConfVolumes [(int) nb]
  REPEAT nb TIMES { [(int) iconf] [(double) volume] }

  Per-conf reference volumes used by the ParticleStress post-processor.

[keyword] SievingSizes
doc: SievingSizes [(int) nb] [(double) size1] [(double) size2] ...

  List of nb sieving sizes used by the ClusterGranulo post-processor.

[keyword] Volume
doc: Volume [(double) value]

  Reference volume used by the ParticleStress post-processor.

# --- shapes

[keyword] name
doc: name [(string) shapeName]

  Set the name of the shape

[keyword] radius
doc: radius [(double) value]

  set the radius of the rounded edges of the shape

[keyword] preCompDone
doc: preCompDone [y/n]

  If yes, the computation of mass properties will not be run
  at the beginning of a computation in Rockable (or in the program shapeSurvey)

[keyword] volume
doc: volume [(double) V]

[keyword] I/m
doc: I/m [(double) I1/m] [(double) I2/m] [(double) I3/m]

[keyword] obb.extent
doc: obb.extent [(double)extent1] [(double)extent2] [(double)extent3]

  The 3 components of the extents in the 3 directions defined by obb.e1, obb.e2 and obb.e3

[keyword] obb.center
doc: obb.center [(vec3r) center]

  Position of the OBB center relative to the mass center of the shape,
  given in the framework (principal direction of inertia) of the shape.

[keyword] obb.e1
doc: obb.e1 [(vec3r) e1]

  Extent unit vector in the first direction

[keyword] obb.e2
doc: obb.e2 [(vec3r) e2]

  Extent unit vector in the second direction

[keyword] obb.e3
doc: obb.e3 [(vec3r) e3]

  Extent unit vector in the third direction

[keyword] fibObbOption
doc: fibObbOption [(int) option]

  Algorithm used to build the OBB of the shape:
    0: covariance-based orientation
    1: minimum-volume strategy
    2: OBB aligned with the axes (AABB) [default]
    3: imposed axis

[keyword] OBBtreeLevel
doc: DEPRECATED!!

[keyword] position
doc: position [(vec3r) center]

  Position of the mass center of the shape, expressed in the local frame of the shape.
  Usually computed automatically (Monte-Carlo integration) when preCompDone is 'n'.

[keyword] orientation
doc: orientation [(quat) Q]

  Angular position (quaternion) of the principal-inertia frame of the shape.
  Usually computed automatically when preCompDone is 'n'.

[keyword] isSurface
doc: isSurface

  Flag (no value) marking the shape as an open surface rather than a closed volume.

[keyword] MCnstep
doc: MCnstep [(int) value]

  Number of steps used in the Monte-Carlo integration of the mass properties
  (volume, mass center, inertia). Clamped internally to the range [1000, 10000000].

[keyword] nv
doc: nv [(int) numberOfVertices]

  REPEAT FOR EACH VERTEX { [(vec3r) position] }
  List of the vertices (sphero-points) of the shape, in the local frame.

[keyword] ne
doc: ne [(int) numberOfEdges]

  REPEAT FOR EACH EDGE { [(int) fromVertex] [(int) toVertex] }
  List of the edges (sphero-segments) connecting two vertices.

[keyword] nf
doc: nf [(int) numberOfFaces]

  REPEAT FOR EACH FACE { [(int) nbNodes] [(int) node1] [(int) node2] ... }
  List of the faces (sphero-polygons), each given by its number of nodes
  followed by the corresponding vertex indices.


